<article>
	<h1>Counter</h1>
	<p>
		A reactive counter with no rust: each button runs a two-line event script that mutates a document field, and the count reads it back. The Rust counterpart is the <code>rsx_site</code> page.
	</p>
	<div bx:scope="counter" bx:style="max-width=Rem(20.0)">
		<p>You have clicked {@doc:count=0} times.</p>
		<div class="design-row">
			<button class="btn btn-filled" bx:click="target.with_field('count', count => count + 1)">More</button>
			<button class="btn btn-tonal" bx:click="target.with_field('count', count => count - 1)">Less</button>
		</div>
	</div>
</article>
